  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1141 AM MDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nAfternoon satellite imagery shows clear skies over the area and\nupstream. So tonight's forecast is looking clear with diminishing\nwinds this evening.\n\nFriday will be warmer than today with high temps well into the\n90s. Winds will be gusty again so fire weather is a concern for\nthe western counties. Hi res models, with support from global\nensemble models, hint at some early morning to afternoon isolated\nrain and thundershowers in south central and central SD. These are\nnot expected to be severe but strong gusty winds are likely with\nany of the stronger cells that develop.\n\nFor the weekend, afternoon highs will remain well above normal for\nearly September. Saturday's highs will be hotter, topping out in\nthe mid to upper 90s for the SD plains, low to mid 90s in NE\nWY. Sunday's highs will be in the upper 80s to mid 90s.\n\nFor now, precip chances on Saturday are mainly contained to the\nBlack Hills and the area to the northeast. But Sunday and Monday,\nan upper level trough looks to swing over Montana and that trough\ncould bring passing thunderstorms to the area. The SPC doesn't\nhave a severe risk out for Sunday or Monday but machine learning\nsevere weather models are hinting at a low end risk of severe \nweather centered over the Black Hills for those days. Stay \nplugged into the forecast through the weekend for updates.\n\nBeyond Monday, low end chances for precip lingers in the forecast\nwith a cooling temperature trend.",
